    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10776" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντοφθαλμ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>look in the face, meet face to face,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. κατὰ πρόσωπον</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				18.46.12
			</span></i>: hence, <i>defy, withstand,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τινα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1.17.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.24.1
			</span></i>, etc., cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Wi.</u>
				12.14
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ τῷ ἀνέμῳ,</span> of a
			ship, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Act.Ap.</u>
				27.15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάθεσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Longin.
					34.4
				</span></i>
			.</div>
